  "note": "Wave 3 verifies the Seestar preview integration against the DB-02 provider running on a fake transport and against fake decoders. Every test is offline and every fixture is synthetic. No hardware, no RTSP connection, no decoder library and no S30Lab code is involved. The app-state shape used for readiness comes from DB-02 fixtures and from the DB-02 mapping code; it has not been observed on a device with an active camera (DB-02 limitation L2).",
  "evidence_classes": {
    "offline": "Deterministic tests against DB-02 over a fake transport, and fake decoders.",
    "hardware": "None. Wave 3 makes no hardware claim; hardware validation is Wave 5."
  },
  "hardware_claims": [],
  "not_claimed": {
    "REQ-058": "Concerns Telemetry samples only (decision D3).",
    "REQ-057": "Fresh-evidence enforcement for safety-sensitive Commands belongs to DB-04.",
    "REQ-060": "Same as REQ-057.",
    "REQ-030": "Simulator Provider obligations are verified by the DB-01 simulator and Wave 2; a fake decoder is not a Simulator Provider.",
    "REQ-031": "Same as REQ-030.",
    "REQ-063": "Same as REQ-030.",
    "hardware": "No hardware evidence of any kind is claimed.",
    "REQ-054": "Outside the DB-03 roadmap coverage (a DB-01/DB-02 boundary). The separation of vendor code from the neutral runtime is recorded as PRV-S3-013."
  },
